      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 3.51,
          "en": "So now that we repeated the basics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.51,
          "end": 5.97,
          "en": "about services and dependency injection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.97,
          "end": 7.77,
          "en": "before we dive deeper,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.77,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "I wanna finish this tasks service here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "And I wanna make sure that we can now also change the status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 16.983,
          "en": "of one of our tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.63,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "Because we have this dropdown here on those tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 24.48,
          "en": "that allow us to pick a different status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "and we then also have a filter that should allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 30.513,
          "en": "to view different tasks depending on their status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 36.18,
          "en": "So in the tasks service, I'll add a new method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.18,
          "end": 39.783,
          "en": "update task status, sounds like a fitting name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "And I expect to get the idea of the task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 45.213,
          "en": "which will be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.74,
          "end": 50.16,
          "en": "And then also the new status that should be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.16,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "And that will be of type task status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "which is a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 59.11,
          "en": "that must be imported from the task model file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "because there it is such a union type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 64.98,
          "en": "a custom union type in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.98,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "where I allow three clearly defined string values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 72.333,
          "en": "as possible values when that type is assigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 77.643,
          "en": "So that is my new status parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 81.87,
          "en": "And then inside of update task status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.87,
          "end": 86.87,
          "en": "and this should be update task status, not update tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.69,
          "end": 92.00999999999999,
          "en": "So inside of this method, I then will reach out to my tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.00999999999999,
          "end": 95.14,
          "en": "and again, call the update method that is built in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 100.5,
          "en": "and pass that function to update where I get my old tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.5,
          "end": 103.41,
          "en": "And the new tasks which I then wanna return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.41,
          "end": 106.743,
          "en": "are the old tasks on which I call map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 111.45,
          "en": "Map is a built-in method that can be executed on arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.45,
          "end": 114.50999999999999,
          "en": "which will produce a new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.50999999999999,
          "end": 117.72,
          "en": "Map then also takes a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "And this function will then be executed on every item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "in that task array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "So on every task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "And the task will be passed in as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 129.813,
          "en": "to this function here automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.22,
          "end": 136.22,
          "en": "Well, and then I want to return an updated task here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.41,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "And for that I'll check if the idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 140.79,
          "en": "of the task I'm currently looking at in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.79,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "that old tasks array, if that is equal to the task ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 147.123,
          "en": "I'm getting here as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 151.07999999999998,
          "en": "If those IDs are equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 154.14,
          "en": "I want to return a new task object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 157.92000000000002,
          "en": "because again, you wanna avoid mutating arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 160.5,
          "en": "of objects directly in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.5,
          "end": 163.74,
          "en": "instead, you should try to create new objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.74,
          "end": 165.93,
          "en": "and arrays and change those.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.93,
          "end": 168.34,
          "en": "So here I am creating a new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.44,
          "end": 172.77,
          "en": "and I'm copying all the old task data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 175.42000000000002,
          "en": "with the spread operator into this new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.7,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "before I then overwrite the status property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 181.83,
          "en": "and set that to the new status value I'm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.83,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "receiving as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "Alternatively, if the IDs do not match,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 191.763,
          "en": "alternatively I'll return the unchanged task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.98,
          "end": 195.63,
          "en": "And here I'm not creating a copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 198.753,
          "en": "because I'm not changing anything about that task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 202.98,
          "en": "So this then updates the tasks array by, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.98,
          "end": 206.31,
          "en": "replacing the old tasks array with a new one where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.31,
          "end": 209.28,
          "en": "for one task where the IDs do match,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 211.803,
          "en": "the task item will have been replaced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.15,
          "end": 214.893,
          "en": "And that is all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.73,
          "end": 219.51,
          "en": "Now since we're working with signals, that information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.51,
          "end": 222.09,
          "en": "that the data changed will be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.09,
          "end": 225.003,
          "en": "to the interested components automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.02,
          "end": 228.75,
          "en": "But of course here in the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.75,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "I still need to adjust the code a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 235.62,
          "en": "because we do have that filter here where users can select",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.62,
          "end": 237.69299999999998,
          "en": "for which tasks they wanna filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 243.33,
          "en": "So they offer in that tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 246.25,
          "en": "I'll actually change tasks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 251.04,
          "en": "and set this to be a computed value with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.04,
          "end": 256.04,
          "en": "of the computed function that is imported from Angular core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 258.24,
          "en": "which is a Signal feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 258.24,
          "end": 260.88,
          "en": "So a feature related to signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 260.88,
          "end": 264.42,
          "en": "because computed will return a new Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 264.42,
          "end": 267.36,
          "en": "but it will return a new computed Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.36,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "which depends on other signals and which will be recomputed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 274.623,
          "en": "whenever any of the dependent signals change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.64,
          "end": 278.43,
          "en": "For that computed takes a function as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.43,
          "end": 280.713,
          "en": "a function that gets no arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.58,
          "end": 283.40999999999997,
          "en": "But in that function, I then want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.40999999999997,
          "end": 287.82,
          "en": "to filter my tasks from the tasks service based on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.82,
          "end": 290.193,
          "en": "the selected filter that has been set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.03,
          "end": 294.06,
          "en": "And actually we can convert selected filter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.06,
          "end": 295.83,
          "en": "to a private property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.83,
          "end": 298.40999999999997,
          "en": "because I'll only use it here in this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.40999999999997,
          "end": 300.24,
          "en": "but that's not too important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.24,
          "end": 301.74,
          "en": "Instead, what is important is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.74,
          "end": 305.58,
          "en": "that in this computed function here, we for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.58,
          "end": 309.51,
          "en": "use a switch statement to switch the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.51,
          "end": 313.083,
          "en": "that is stored in the selected filter Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 316.662,
          "en": "And since I'm using a Signal here in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.662,
          "end": 321.39,
          "en": "which I'm passing to compute it, Angular will register this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 321.39,
          "end": 325.26,
          "en": "and set up a subscription and recompute that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.26,
          "end": 327.753,
          "en": "whenever the selected filter value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 329.88,
          "end": 332.61,
          "en": "So here I'm switching on that value that's stored in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 337.2,
          "en": "that Signal and in case the value is all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 337.2,
          "end": 338.79,
          "en": "which is one of the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 338.79,
          "end": 341.43,
          "en": "that can be chosen here in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 341.43,
          "end": 344.058,
          "en": "in case the value is all I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 344.058,
          "end": 349,
          "en": "to return this tasks service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 349.98,
          "end": 354.84000000000003,
          "en": "all tasks, which I guess makes sense if we're requesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 354.84000000000003,
          "end": 358.08299999999997,
          "en": "to see all tasks, I wanna return all tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 359.49,
          "end": 361.47,
          "en": "And this is another Signal being read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 361.47,
          "end": 365.22,
          "en": "So now computed will recalculate also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 365.22,
          "end": 368.13,
          "en": "when all tasks changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 368.13,
          "end": 372.06,
          "en": "So it will recalculate either if the selected filter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 372.06,
          "end": 375.303,
          "en": "changes or if the all tasks value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 376.68,
          "end": 380.52,
          "en": "So that is one case, but it's of course not the only one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 380.52,
          "end": 385.52,
          "en": "The second case is that the user selected this open option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 386.52,
          "end": 389.7,
          "en": "the offer here, my case is open,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 389.7,
          "end": 392.8,
          "en": "and here I return this tasks service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 393.9,
          "end": 394.95,
          "en": "all tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 394.95,
          "end": 399.93,
          "en": "But now I want to filter those tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 399.93,
          "end": 404.7,
          "en": "And for that we can call the built-in filter method on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 404.7,
          "end": 407.76,
          "en": "that value that is returned by all tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 407.76,
          "end": 411.54,
          "en": "Since all tasks will return an array of tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 411.54,
          "end": 414.72,
          "en": "we can call filter on that since that's a built-in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 414.72,
          "end": 416.823,
          "en": "that can be called on any array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 418.08,
          "end": 420.33,
          "en": "And filter then takes a function as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 420.33,
          "end": 423.36,
          "en": "which will be executed for every array item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 423.36,
          "end": 426.09,
          "en": "And we should return true here if we want to keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 426.09,
          "end": 430.41,
          "en": "that item in the new array that will be returned by filter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 430.41,
          "end": 433.47,
          "en": "or false if we wanna drop it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 433.47,
          "end": 436.113,
          "en": "so that we can create a filtered array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 437.1,
          "end": 438.42,
          "en": "Well in here, I simply want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.42,
          "end": 443.133,
          "en": "to check if the task status is equal to open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 444.989,
          "end": 448.59,
          "en": "Because if the case is open, I only want to get the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 448.59,
          "end": 450.093,
          "en": "where the status is open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 452.7,
          "end": 457.7,
          "en": "The next case is that the user selected in-progress.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 459.27,
